From: qr0n <77075118+qr0n@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:40:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] [Pascal] GPTQ/AutoRound without Marlin, and an sm_60
 exllama GPTQ kernel

- auto_gptq / INC: only require Marlin on sm_75+, so pre-Turing falls back
  to the exllama kernel instead of refusing to load.
- q_gemm.cu: on cc < 7.0 the 4-bit exllama GEMM masks nibbles straight into
  subnormal fp16 (q * 2^-24, exact; HFMA2 is full rate on subnormals on
  sm_60), pre-scales activations per 128-row slice and removes the zero point
  in fp32 per 32 rows. M=4 GEMM ~300 -> ~390 GB/s. VLLM_GPTQ_SM60_KERNEL=0
  selects the stock kernel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
